// DfCoverage.pkg - hit counters for instrumented DataFlex source.
//
// Used only by an instrumented *copy* of a workspace's source; nothing here belongs in an
// application. The instrumenter inserts `Send DfCovHit <id>` at the entry of every basic block.
//
// This package is included as the very first line of the generated program, ahead of the
// program's own `Use Windows.pkg`, because code appearing early in a `.src` -- an error trap
// object, for instance -- is instrumented too and calls DfCovHit before any framework package
// has been compiled.
//
// `Use UI` below is what makes that position work, and it is not optional. Declaring a global
// procedure before the base runtime is loaded compiles without complaint but registers nothing,
// so every later `Send DfCovHit` fails with "Forward reference not resolved MSG_DFCOVHIT".
// Pulling the runtime in here keeps this package self-sufficient, so it does not matter what the
// instrumented program's own `Use` block happens to start with.
//
// Anything needing the *file* runtime -- writing the counts out -- lives in DfCoverageWrite.pkg,
// which is included later, beside the test application object.
//
// Two further choices, both about the hot path:
//
//   * `DfCovHit` is a *global* procedure, so a probe needs no object handle in scope. That keeps
//     the inserted line to a single `Send` no matter where it lands.
//
//   * The counters live in a `Global_Variable Integer[]`, not an array property. DataFlex gets
//     and sets array properties whole, with copy-on-write, so a property would copy the entire
//     counter array on every single hit - fatal for something called millions of times in a test
//     run.

Use UI

// Hit counts, indexed by probe id. DataFlex grows an integer array on first indexed write, so no
// size needs to be declared up front.
Global_Variable Integer[] gaiDfCovHits

/// Records one execution of the probe with this id.
Procedure DfCovHit Global Integer iProbe
    // A DataFlex array grows on an indexed *write* but raises an error on an indexed *read* past
    // its end, so a counter has to exist before it can be incremented. Without this guard the
    // very first probe to fire takes down the run through the error trap, which exits the process
    // before any counts are written -- and the coverage report is simply empty, with the real
    // cause only visible in the program's error file.
    //
    // The array reaches full size once every probe has fired once, so the second branch is taken
    // at most once per probe no matter how long the run is.
    If (iProbe < SizeOfArray(gaiDfCovHits)) Begin
        Move (gaiDfCovHits[iProbe] + 1) to gaiDfCovHits[iProbe]
    End
    Else Begin
        Move 1 to gaiDfCovHits[iProbe]
    End
End_Procedure

/// Clears every counter. Useful when one program runs several suites in sequence.
Procedure DfCovReset Global
    Integer[] aiEmpty
    Move aiEmpty to gaiDfCovHits
End_Procedure
